  "weeklyExtras": {
    "week": 7,
    "tagline": "Week 7 News · Full Rankings · Luck Gaps · Player Impact",
    "kicker": "GFL Insider · Week 7",
    "headline": "THE LEAGUE SPLIT OPEN",
    "deck": "Flint finally broke through, Eskimo Brothers stole the weekly crown, California reached 6-1 with the league’s eighth-best all-play mark, and the strongest scoring team lurks in third place. Seven weeks in, the standings are no longer telling the whole truth.",
    "story": [
      "Week 7 redrew the map. Eskimo Brothers posted 136.32 to take the weekly high point and move to 5-2, while Flint Tropics erupted for 134.72 to secure its first victory. Flint did not merely escape the basement. It finished second in the entire league for the week and beat Medford MountainMen despite Medford scoring 112.30, the fourth-best total on the slate.",
      "The top of the standings now contains two 6-1 teams, but the underlying profiles are wildly different. Redwood Murder is 6-1 with the league’s fifth-best all-play record at 42-35. California Un-Named Team is also 6-1, yet sits eighth in all-play at 35-42 and eighth in total points. California has converted about 3.18 all-play expected wins into six actual wins, the largest positive record gap in the league.",
      "Sullco MethMouths may be the most complete team behind the leaders. At 5-2, Sullco ranks first in total points with 809.40 and first in all-play at 52-25. Turbulent Ticklesh!ts remains second in both categories, but a 68.08-point collapse dropped Ticklesh!ts to 4-3. The league’s two strongest scoring profiles now sit third and fifth in the official standings.",
      "The other side of schedule fortune is brutal. Flint Tropics is 1-6 despite ranking seventh in PF and seventh in all-play; its opponents have scored 838.00 points. Medford MountainMen has faced 846.32 points, the league’s highest total. Both teams have taken punishment far beyond what their own records alone reveal.",
      "The week was defined by separation and reversal. Eskimo Brothers and Flint Tropics finished first and second in scoring, Space Cadets delivered the third-highest total to upset Off Boys, and the league’s second-ranked season-long scoring team finished last for the week. At this stage of the season, one extreme result can reorder an entire division race."
    ],
    "awards": [
      {
        "emoji": "🏆",
        "title": "Week 7 High Point",
        "team": "Eskimo Brothers",
        "detail": "136.32 points, edging Flint Tropics by 1.60 for the weekly crown."
      },
      {
        "emoji": "🌴",
